reating a top-level authorship_resolution -> authorship import cycle.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.332,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["authorship.py currently uses module-level `import subprocess` (L24) and calls `subprocess.run(...)` unqualified inside the five functions","test_authorship_resolver_git_flags.py:32 monkeypatches `authorship.subprocess` then calls `authorship.resolve_event_commit`, so the moved code must read the runner from the authorship module, not from authorship_resolution's own binding","Plan bullet 2: authorship.py must 'Import and re-export all five names from authorship.py' [sic — from authorship_resolution], creating a top-level authorship -> authorship_resolution edge; the seam mechanism adds an authorship_resolution -> authorship edge","The existing code already uses a lazy import for exactly this reason (`from rebar._commands._seam import tracker_dir` inside each function, L158/336/421/491) — the plan does not extend that pattern to the authorship reference"],"finding":"The subprocess-seam mechanism ('git subprocess calls in the moved implementation resolve the runner through the live authorship.subprocess compatibility attribute at call time') requires authorship_resolution.py to hold a reference to the authorship module, while authorship.py must import the five names FROM authorship_resolution at module top. That is a circular import. The plan specifies call-time ATTRIBUTE lookup but does not specify that authorship_resolution must obtain the authorship module reference via a lazy/in-function import to avoid an import-time cycle.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd013693e30e1c1e6","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Preserve the established subprocess monkeypatch seam explicitly'","norm_id":"n4ce70ae074d31db3","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["At import time, `import rebar.attest.authorship` triggers `from authorship_resolution import ...`, which (if authorship_resolution imports authorship at top level) re-enters a partially-initialized authorship module and raises ImportError/AttributeError","attest/__init__.py:22 imports authorship at package init, so any cycle fails the whole package import"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the moved functions, replace the direct `subprocess.run(...)` with a call-time lazy import of the authorship module and read `.subprocess` off it: `import rebar.attest.authorship as _authorship; _authorship.subprocess.run(...)`. Do NOT add a module-level `import rebar.attest.authorship` to authorship_resolution.py (that reintroduces the cycle).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the reference inventory for all five moved symbols using Serena `find_referencing_symbols` (plus a string grep for setattr/getattr/parametrization sites), and fold the omitted consumers tests/unit/_opcert_helpers.py and tests/unit/test_opcert_storage.py (both call authorship.build_introducing_co